	(text "U9 74LVC1G74GT BOOTSEL latch: reset button net M_RSTB (S1, R50) clocks BOOT into Q;\nRP2350B RUN follows via R34 10 kΩ / C66 1 µF (~10 ms later), so D = BOOT is stable.\nC83 100 nF holds ~RD low at cold power-on so Q clears to L (J14 / BOOTSEL).\nBOOT held during reset -> Q = L -> U5 routes RP2350B USB to J14 (PC / BOOTSEL).\nNormal reset -> Q = H -> USB to the CH334F hub (USB-A ports).\nX2 low forces J14 (RD), X3 low forces the hub (SD); never both low."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 172.72 54.61 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1200ed35-0109-4ec6-8836-7c55ce76d4e0")
	)
	(text "LD2 WS2812B on RP2350B GPIO43, powered from VBUS via D4 (~4.4 V)\nso the 3.3 V DIN still meets its VIH. R51 330 Ω: data series."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 82.55 157.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f4ea9a7c-8f28-4c54-a6c6-6c38a9f348fd")
	)
	(text "U12 PCF8574 I/O expander on the master I2C (GPIO2 SDA / GPIO3 SCL), address 0x20.\nPCF8574 is a 100 kHz part: run the whole I2C bus at 100 kHz.\nPorts are quasi-bidirectional (strong low, weak high); all high after power-on.\nP0 = S_RUN: RP2350A RUN via R56 1 kΩ (R20 pull-up, S4 button).  P2 / P3 = USB mux overrides.\nP1 = SD card detect (J7 pin 9).  P5 spare (RM2 WL_ON moved to slave GPIO28).\nP4, P6, P7 spare.  Firmware: write all 8 bits at init, then pulse P3 low once (hub)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 55.88 54.61 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "fb24ee73-f680-4c9c-8c22-98db004fc03d")
	)
